{
  "id": "06089_fumitsukeru",
  "headword": "{踏|ふ}みつける",
  "reading": "ふみつける",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (ichidan)",
  "gloss": "to trample, to step on",
  "conjugation": {
    "type": "ichidan",
    "stem": "{踏|ふ}みつけ"
  },
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to trample, to step on hard",
      "explanation": "To step on something forcefully, pressing it down with one's foot."
    },
    {
      "sense_number": 2,
      "gloss": "to trample on (figurative)",
      "explanation": "To violate, disregard, or treat with contempt someone's rights, feelings, or dignity."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "06089_fumitsukeru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{虫|むし}を{踏|ふ}みつけてしまった。",
      "english": "I accidentally stepped on a bug.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06089_fumitsukeru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{落|お}ち{葉|ば}を{踏|ふ}みつけながら{歩|ある}く。",
      "english": "Walking while treading on fallen leaves.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06089_fumitsukeru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{怒|おこ}った{子|こ}どもが{地面|じめん}を{足|あし}で{踏|ふ}みつけていた。",
      "english": "The angry child was stomping on the ground with their feet.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06089_fumitsukeru_ex4",
      "japanese": "{人|ひと}の{尊厳|そんげん}を{踏|ふ}みつけてはいけない。",
      "english": "You must not trample on people's dignity.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06089_fumitsukeru_ex5",
      "japanese": "{弱|よわ}い{者|もの}の{権利|けんり}を{踏|ふ}みつけるような{社会|しゃかい}であってはならない。",
      "english": "We must not be a society that tramples on the rights of the weak.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06089_fumitsukeru_ex6",
      "japanese": "{相手|あいて}の{気持|きも}ちを{踏|ふ}みつけるような{発言|はつげん}は{許|ゆる}されない。",
      "english": "Remarks that trample on the other person's feelings are unacceptable.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive). No pair verb.\n\nCOMPOUND STRUCTURE: {踏|ふ}む (to step on) + つける (to attach/press). The compound emphasizes pressing down firmly.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n・{虫|むし}を{踏|ふ}みつける (step on a bug)\n・{足|あし}で{踏|ふ}みつける (trample with one's foot)\n・{権利|けんり}を{踏|ふ}みつける (trample on rights)\n・{尊厳|そんげん}を{踏|ふ}みつける (trample on dignity)\n\nUsage note: The figurative sense is common in formal writing and speeches about human rights or ethics.",
